    "comments": [
      {
        "id": "ls-c1",
        "x": -340,
        "y": -330,
        "text": "LOW-SIDE SWITCH WITH A 3.3 V LOGIC-LEVEL FET (TI CSD17382F4)\nV2 stands in for a 3.3 V microcontroller pin. When it goes high, M1 turns\non and connects the bottom of the load (R1) to ground, so the load gets 12 V.\nThe CSD17382F4 is fully on from about 2.5 V (around 60 mOhm), so a 3.3 V\npin can drive it directly. M1 uses TI's own SPICE model, body diode included."
      },
      {
        "id": "ls-c2",
        "x": -340,
        "y": 65,
        "text": "R2 (100 Ohm) limits the current spike into the gate when the pin switches.\nR3 (100k) holds the gate low, so M1 stays off while the microcontroller\nis still booting and its pin is floating."
      },
      {
        "id": "ls-c3",
        "x": 230,
        "y": -200,
        "text": "Try it: run (Ctrl+B), press P, then click\nthe drain wire above M1 and the wire\nbetween V2 and R2.\nDrain: 12 V when off, about 30 mV when on\n(0.5 A through about 60 mOhm)."
      }
    ]
  },
